  "id": "Compound::DB01033 - Gene::9153",
  "verbalization": "Mercaptopurine is likely to interact with Slc28a2 through a series of molecular and functional connections. The evidence suggests that Mercaptopurine binds to Slc28a3 or Slc29a2, both of which are involved in nucleoside transport. Slc28a3 and Slc29a2 are both part of the Slc28 family of transporters, which are responsible for the transport of nucleosides and purines across cellular membranes. Since Slc28a2 is involved in the participation of these transport activities, it is plausible that Mercaptopurine influences Slc28a2 through its interaction with these transporters. The evidence supports a mechanism where Mercaptopurine modulates the activity of Slc28a2 by affecting the transport of nucleosides, potentially through a direct or indirect interaction at the transporter level. This integrated pathway highlights the role of Slc28a2 in nucleoside transport and suggests that Mercaptopurine may exert its effects on this transporter, possibly through a complex interplay involving multiple transporters.",
